122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (2025 has been a year that brought me back, again and again, to the reason BetterLife exists.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (I have stood in places where climate change is not a conversation, but a condition people are forced to live through. I have met mothers who spend entire nights standing with their children because floods have taken their homes, and still wake up to try again. I have sat with young people in refugee settlements who are full of ideas, full of energy, but locked out of opportunity. And I have walked with farmers who are not failing because they are not working hard, but because the seasons they once understood no longer exist in the same way.This is the reality we are working in.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (In 2025, BetterLife International reached over 112,000 people across Uganda, South Sudan, Tanzania, and Ghana. But beyond the numbers, we made a conscious decision to go deeper to focus on solutions that are not temporary, but ones that begin to shift the conditions people are living in.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (Through the SMILES Livelihood Programme, we saw what happens when people are given a real chance. Young people started small businesses. Women came together and built support systems for each other.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (Annual Report 2025)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (BetterLife International)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E ( Families that once depended on aid began to find their own footing again. It was not immediate, and it was not easy, but it was real. And in many ways, it was the beginning of something bigger.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (At the same time, we expanded Soilla, because we understood that sometimes the biggest gap is not effort, but access. Farmers are doing everything they can, but without the right information, at the right time, they remain vulnerable. Through Soilla, we are starting to change that slowly, but meaningfully.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (What continues to shape this work is how close we remain to the communities we serve. We do not work from a distance. We listen. We sit in the reality, even when it is uncomfortable. And we build solutions together. That is what makes this work different. We are still growing. We are still learning. But we are committed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (To our partners, to our supporters, and most importantly, to the communities we walk with thank you for trusting us. The challenges are real. But so are the people. And that is what keeps us going.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
