182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (The operational context in 2025 continued to be shaped by increasing climate variability, economic pressures, and displacement across the regions where BetterLife works. In Uganda and South Sudan, refugee populations remained particularly vulnerable to both environmental and socio-economic shocks. Across all countries of operation, smallholder farmers faced unpredictable weather patterns, reduced yields, and limited access to climate-informed agricultural support.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (In response, BetterLife adopted a strategy focused on resilience, inclusion, and innovation, strengthening programmes that simultaneously address environmental sustainability and economic empowerment. This approach ensured that communities were not only supported to cope with immediate challenges, but also equipped with the tools and systems necessary to adapt and thrive in the long term.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
