219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (In 2025, BetterLife International focused on delivering integrated solutions that address both environmental sustainability and economic empowerment across Uganda, South Sudan, Tanzania, and Ghana. Our programmes supported farmers, youth, and refugee communities through climate-smart agriculture, digital innovation, and livelihood development initiatives. Through the SMILES Programme, vulnerable populations were equipped with practical skills and supported to establish small businesses, enabling them to generate income and improve household stability. At the same time, the expansion of the Soilla platform allowed farmers to access critical agricultural information, improving productivity and strengthening resilience to climate variability.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (Our environmental efforts continued through community-based recycling initiatives and sustainable farming practices, reducing environmental degradation while creating opportunities for local income generation. Across all programmes, we prioritized community participation, ensuring that solutions were locally driven and sustainable beyond project implementation. By combining climate action with livelihood support, BetterLife International continues to build systems that not only respond to immediate needs but also strengthen long-term resilience and economic independence for vulnerable communities.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
