/P 71 0 R
/E (BetterLife International aims to expand its climate resilience and livelihood programmes by scaling the SMILES initiative and strengthening the Soilla platform across more communities and regions. The organization will continue to invest in practical solutions that support farmers, youth, and refugee populations through skills development, digital innovation, and community-based systems. By strengthening partnerships, improving programme delivery, and enhancing monitoring and learning systems, BetterLife seeks to increase its impact while ensuring long-term sustainability. These efforts will contribute to building resilient communities that are better equipped to adapt to climate challenges and create sustainable economic opportunities.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (BetterLife International continues to strengthen climate resilience and inclusive livelihoods across vulnerable communities by expanding practical, community-driven solutions that address both environmental and economic challenges. Through the growth of the SMILES Programme and the scale-up of the Soilla platform, the organization is supporting farmers, youth, and refugee populations with the skills, tools, and opportunities needed to build sustainable futures. By investing in innovation, strengthening partnerships, and empowering local communities, BetterLife is creating pathways for long-term resilience, improved food security, and economic independence across the regions in which it operates.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (BetterLife International will focus on strengthening regional coordination and expanding its presence into new communities through scalable, locally led programmes. The organization will invest in building stronger community institutions, supporting cooperative systems, and enhancing access to markets for small enterprises. Efforts will also be directed toward strengthening youth-led innovation and increasing opportunities for women in climate and livelihood initiatives. By deepening collaboration with governments and partners, BetterLife aims to create more inclusive systems that support long-term growth, resilience, and shared economic progress across the communities it serves)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
